firmware-studio (1.0.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Install the HiFiBerry repository signing key into /etc/apt/keyrings and use
    signed-by= instead of [trusted=yes], so apt no longer warns about a missing
    key. Setup script and README updated accordingly.
  * Depend on curl and ca-certificates (used to fetch the signing key).

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 09 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0000

firmware-studio (1.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add firmware-studio-setup: one-shot setup for stock Raspberry Pi OS
    (adds the HiFiBerry apt repo, installs the package, configures config.txt
    and frees the serial UART for UPDI flashing).
  * README: document adding the apt repo, the package to install and the
    config.txt settings.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 09 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000

firmware-studio (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package.
  * Ship Studio DAC8x microcontroller firmware v0.0.2
    (studiodac8x-0.0.2.hex).
  * Add flash-studio-dac8x helper to flash firmware over UPDI via pymcuprog.

